          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How will you multiply two numbers given in Roman numerals, without converting them to Hindu numerals? Try to find the product of the following pairs of landmark numbers: V × L, L × D, V × D, VII × IX."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.289,
            0.318,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " V × L = CCL"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.309,
            0.475,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "L × D = MMM…M (25 times)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.328,
            0.337,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "V × D = MMD"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.348,
            0.357,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "VII × IX = LXIII"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
